trategy and Resources Committee","date":"2026-07-23","category":"treasury","fy":"2025/26"}],"calendar":{"upcoming":[{"date":"2026-09-24","committee":"Strategy and Resources Committee","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.maldon.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-08","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee (meeting as the Crime and Disorder Committee)","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.maldon.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-22","committee":"Council","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.maldon.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-12","committee":"Performance, Governance and Audit Committee","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.maldon.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-19","committee":"Strategy and Resources Committee","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.maldon.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-26","committee":"Strategy and Resources Committee","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.maldon.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-12-03","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Provisional","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.maldon.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-12-10","committee":"Council","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.maldon.gov.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-07-23","committee":"Strategy and Resources Committee","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.maldon.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-30","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed; SPECIAL","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.maldon.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-03","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.maldon.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-10","committee":"Council","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.maldon.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-17","committee":"Performance, Governance and Audit Committee","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.maldon.gov.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Maldon faces audit recovery after three years without account sign-off","lead":"The council's accounts have not received auditor sign-off for more than three years, because the balance sheet position could not be fully verified. External auditors have issued disclaimed opinions for this entire period \u2014 meaning they were unable to form any opinion on whether the accounts are correct. The auditors have now assessed the council as 'B' rated under the government's rebuild framework, with recovery targeted by November 2027. The council must fully reconcile its balance sheet across the six-year period from March 2021 through March 2027 to enable auditors to sign off the accounts once more.","iso":"2026-09-17","paper_title":"Annual Governance Statement Actions Update","paper_url":"https://democracy.maldon.gov.uk/documents/s42732/42732.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Strategy and Resources Committee","paper_title":"Appendix 4","paper_url":"https://democracy.maldon.gov.uk/documents/s42841/42841.pdf","headline":"Revised budget requires \u00a3836k drawdown from General Fund reserves, up \u00a3110k from original plan","detail":"The reconciliation shows the council drawing \u00a3836k from General Fund reserves to balance the revised budget, an increase of \u00a3110k from the \u00a3726k planned in the original budget. This covers the shortfall between net service expenditure of \u00a314,137k and revenue from council tax (\u00a38,695k), business rates (\u00a33,070k), and government grants (\u00a31,536k), meaning the council is funding 5.9% of its operating budget from reserve depletion.","category":"reserves","matters":"Lenders assess whether a council funds ongoing operations from sustainable revenue or from reserves. Drawing down reserves to cover operating shortfalls signals structural funding pressure and reduces financial flexibility, affecting credit risk.","figures":"Original General Fund transfer: \u00a3726k. Revised General Fund transfer: \u00a3836k. Revenue funding (council tax plus business rates plus grants): \u00a313,301k. Revised net service expenditure: \u00a314,137k.","quote":"Transfer (from)/to General Fund (726) 0 (110) (836)","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Strategy and Resources Committee","paper_title":"8 Medium-Term Financial Strategy Update","paper_url":"https://democracy.maldon.gov.uk/documents/s42842/42842.pdf","headline":"Local government reorganisation timing delayed from April 2028 to April 2029 with risk of further deferral, creating going-concern uncertainty","detail":"The council previously expected LGR to end its statutory existence in April 2028. A recent government decision review has created uncertainty. The council now assumes April 2029 but must also plan for LGR to be deferred or delayed, meaning it may need to sustain itself financially beyond the MTFS period with no certainty of merger.","category":"governance","matters":"A lender must understand whether this council will continue to exist and operate independently; the timing of merger directly affects whether the council must plan for long-term financial sustainability or manage a wind-down, and uncertainty about either outcome complicates financial planning","figures":"April 2028 (previous expectation), April 2029 (assumed date)","quote":"Previously, LGR had been expected to lead to the end of the Council as a statutory public body in April 2028 \u2013 which caps financial risks and opens alternative ways to handle those risks. However, the recently announced review of the decision means that there remains some uncertainty over the timing of LGR.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Strategy and Resources Committee","paper_title":"8 Medium-Term Financial Strategy Update","paper_url":"https://democracy.maldon.gov.uk/documents/s42842/42842.pdf","headline":"Unspecified spending cuts must close growing funding gaps of \u00a31.4m\u2013\u00a35.5m by 2029/30; reserve fallback is available but size unknown","detail":"The MTFS projects funding gaps of \u00a31.4m (2027/28), \u00a32.6m (2028/29), and \u00a35.5m (2029/30) if spending grows as currently budgeted. The strategy proposes to close these through unspecified 'scrutiny of planned spending' and cost control, with 'the balance being funded from general reserves' if reductions fall short. No specific service cuts are identified.","category":"reserves","matters":"A lender cannot assess whether this council's strategy is credible without knowing what savings it will make and what reserve balances are available; a \u00a35.5m gap is material relative to annual funding of \u00a311.5m, and the lack of specific spending cuts raises questions about how the gap will actually be closed","figures":"\u00a31,424.7k (2027/28), \u00a32,622.7k (2028/29), \u00a35,481.4k (2029/30)","quote":"with the balance being funded from general reserves","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Strategy and Resources Committee","paper_title":"8 Medium-Term Financial Strategy Update","paper_url":"https://democracy.maldon.gov.uk/documents/s42842/42842.pdf","headline":"Government funding reduced by \u00a3100k year-on-year with no inflationary growth, creating \u00a31.5m structural gap in 2026/27 and flat cash through 2027\u20132028","detail":"Government funding falls by \u00a3100k between 2025/26 and 2026/27, and the council loses \u00a3300k that it had previously expected for inflationary pressures. This \u00a3400k loss coincides with \u00a31.1m in actual inflationary cost pressures, creating a \u00a31.5m structural gap in 2026/27. The council's funding remains flat at around \u00a311.5m per year through 2027/28 and 2028/29 despite ongoing inflation.","category":"income","matters":"A lender needs to assess whether a council can sustain services when funding shrinks while input costs rise; flat cash in inflationary times constrains financial viability and forces difficult choices between service reduction and reserve depletion","figures":"\u00a3100k annual reduction, \u00a3300k lost inflationary growth, \u00a3400k total loss, \u00a31.1m annual inflation pressures, \u00a31.5m 2026/27 structural gap","quote":"The loss of \u00a3100k of cash plus the absence of inflationary funding growth of \u00a3300k indicates an overall funding loss of \u00a3400k. Inflationary pressures usually amount to around \u00a31.1m year-to-year.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Strategy and Resources Committee","paper_title":"Appendix 1","paper_url":"https://democracy.maldon.gov.uk/documents/s42843/42843.pdf","headline":"Investment income forecast to fall by 56%, from \u00a3800k to \u00a3350k.","detail":"Projected investment income declines from \u00a3800.0k in 2026/27 to \u00a3350.0k by 2029/30\u2014a planned, deliberate reduction over the MTFS period.","category":"income","matters":"Investment income is discretionary revenue; losing more than half of it further constrains the council's ability to support spending at a time when government funding is also falling.","figures":"Investment Income: \u00a3800.0k (2026/27), \u00a3350.0k (2029/30)","quote":"Investment Income (800.0) (600.0) (500.0) (350.0)","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-17"},"name":"Maldon DC","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-22","since_iso":"2026-08-23","distress":false,"headline":"The council must fully reconcile its entire balance sheet from March 2021 through March 2027 to resolve disclaimed opinions","lead":"This requirement indicates that underlying accounting systems or controls have not been able to maintain proper reconciliation, and the scope of work (a 6-year reconstruction) suggests material historical accounting issues","also":["4 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Strategy and Resources Committee on 2026-09-24","n_findings":5,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"7 External Audit - Building Back Assurance","top_paper_url":"https://democracy.maldon.gov.uk/documents/s42773/42773.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":80,"news_drafts_total":1}}